se. Many experimental pieces are very short, and many classical pieces (symphonies, operas) are very long. Duration is not a defining characteristic that separates the two universally.\n\nThe most accurate comparison highlighting a key difference between the two genres is that experimental music frequently involves a departure from the strict formal and harmonic conventions that define much of traditional classical music.\n\nTherefore, option A provides the strongest contrast based on established musical definitions.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
